# Tomik, Distinguished Advokist: "Lands on the battlefield and land cards in graveyards can't be the targets of spells or
# abilities your opponents control" (CR 601.2c, 602.2b) - any land and any graveyard's land card, the opponent's own too. Bot1
# casts Tomik (flying) on turn 1 with Black Lotus. On turn 3 Bot1, no opponent of its own, aims Strip Mine at Bot2's Swamp and
# Cling to Dust at its own Strip Mine in its graveyard. On turn 4 Bot2 can't aim Strip Mine at Bot1's Plains or its own Strip
# Mine, Deathrite Shaman at the Swamp in its own graveyard, or Cling to Dust at that Swamp; Cling to Dust still exiles Bot1's
# Black Lotus, a nonland card. Bolted, Tomik is gone, and Bot2's Deathrite exiles the Swamp and Strip Mine destroys the Plains.

